      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "With the release of groups this should be easy to implement now: \n\nHave a setting for \"shared home\" where you chose a home-world and a home-group/\"family\".\n\nWhen going home we check if these settings are set and if so go through your friends in the home-group checking if their location is a joinable instance of the home world, if one is found you join there.\n\nIf none are found you open a new instance and with the access-rights set to allow for your home-group.\n\nEasy as that really...We could probably even code a little script for that as a community...",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-11-10T18:21:54.803Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A feature where you can setup a home world with multiple people so when a homeworld session is created the other people going in to their home world will join the same session as you. The idea of logging in to a familiar place with your friends already hanging out there is amazing in my opinion.",
